text:
Bagian Kedua
PPT PKBGA
Pasal 6
PPT PKBGA sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 5 ayat (1) huruf a dibentuk oleh Bupati sesuai dengan Peraturan Perundang-undangan.
Keanggotaan PPT PKBGA sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) terdiri dari: unsur Pemerintah Daerah;
instansi vertikal;
lembaga non pemerintah;
institusi pelayanan kesehatan;
aparat penegak hukum;
tenaga profesi;
relawan pendamping;
pekerja sosial;
rohaniwan; dan layanan rehabilitasi sosial.
Keanggotaan Tim PPT PKBGA sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2) ditetapkan dengan Keputusan Bupati.

translated_text:
Part Two
PPT PKBGA
Article 6
PPT PKBGA as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (1) letter a is established by the Regent in accordance with the Laws and Regulations.
The membership of PPT PKBGA as referred to in paragraph (1) consists of: elements of Regional Government;
vertical agencies;
non-governmental institutions;
health service institutions;
law enforcement apparatus;
professional personnel;
companion volunteers;
social workers;
religious leaders; and social rehabilitation services.
The membership of the PPT PKBGA Team as referred to in paragraph (2) is determined by Regent's Decree.

text:
Pasal 9
PPT PKBGA sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 5 ayat (1) huruf a mempunyai tugas: mengupayakan pencegahan;
memberikan pelayanan pengaduan;
memberikan pelayanan kesehatan;
memberikan pelayanan rehabilitasi sosial;
memberikan pelayanan bantuan dan penegakan hukum;
memberikan pelayanan pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial;
melakukan koordinasi dan kerjasama;
mengupayakan peningkatan partisipasi masyarakat; dan melakukan monitoring dan pelaporan.

translated_text:
Article 9
PPT PKBGA as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (1) letter a has the duties of: pursuing prevention;
providing complaint services;
providing health services;
providing social rehabilitation services;
providing legal assistance and enforcement services;
providing repatriation and social reintegration services;
conducting coordination and cooperation;
pursuing increased community participation; and conducting monitoring and reporting.

text:
Pasal 10
Upaya Pencegahan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 9 huruf a meliputi: menyelenggarakan komunikasi, informasi, dan edukasi tentang kekerasan berbasis gender dan anak;
mensosialisasikan peraturan perundang-undangan yang berkaitan dengan kekerasan berbasis gender dan anak.

translated_text:
Article 10
Prevention Efforts as referred to in Article 9 letter a include: conducting communication, information, and education about gender-based and child violence;
socializing laws and regulations related to gender-based and child violence.

text:
Pasal 11
Pelayanan Pengaduan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 9 huruf b meliputi: pelayanan pengaduan langsung;
pelayanan pengaduan melalui telepon;
pelayanan pengaduan melalui surat;
pelayanan pengaduan dari rujukan;
pelayanan penjangkauan korban; dan pelayanan pengaduan melalui media sosial yang dikelola PPT PKBGA dan UPPTK.

translated_text:
Article 11
Complaint Services as referred to in Article 9 letter b include: direct complaint services;
complaint services through telephone;
complaint services through letter;
complaint services from referrals;
victim outreach services; and complaint services through social media managed by PPT PKBGA and UPPTK.

text:
Pasal 12
Pelayanan Kesehatan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 9 huruf c meliputi: pelayanan medis;
pelayanan medis psikiatrik; dan pelayanan medicolegal, meliputi visum et repertum (VER), visum et psikiatrum (VEP), dan identifikasi deoxyribonucleic acid (DNA).

translated_text:
Article 12
Health Services as referred to in Article 9 letter c include: medical services;
psychiatric medical services; and medicolegal services, including visum et repertum (VER), visum et psikiatrum (VEP), and deoxyribonucleic acid (DNA) identification.

text:
Pasal 13
Pelayanan Rehabilitasi Sosial sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 9 huruf d meliputi: pelayanan konseling awal;
pelayanan konseling lanjutan;
penyediaan rumah aman; dan pelayanan bimbingan rohani.
Rehabilitasi Sosial dilaksanakan secara terpadu.

translated_text:
Article 13
Social Rehabilitation Services as referred to in Article 9 letter d include: initial counseling services;
follow-up counseling services;
provision of safe houses; and spiritual guidance services.
Social Rehabilitation is implemented in an integrated manner.

text:
Pasal 14
Pelayanan Bantuan dan Penegakan Hukum sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 9 huruf e terdiri dari: pelayanan bantuan hukum meliputi bantuan pendampingan hukum litigasi dan bantuan pendampingan hukum non litigasi;
pelayanan penegakan hukum meliputi penegakan hukum di tingkat kepolisian, penegakan hukum di tingkat kejaksaan, dan penegakan hukum di tingkat pengadilan;
pelayanan penegakan hukum di tingkat kepolisian sebagaimana dimaksud pada huruf b meliputi penegakan hukum pada proses penyelidikan dan/atau penyidikan;
pelayanan penegakan hukum di tingkat kejaksaan sebagaimana dimaksud pada huruf b meliputi penegakan hukum pada proses pra penuntutan dan penuntutan; dan pelayanan penegakan hukum di tingkat pengadilan sebagaimana dimaksud pada huruf b meliputi penegakan hukum pada tahap pra persidangan, persidangan, dan penjatuhan putusan.

translated_text:
Article 14
Legal Assistance and Law Enforcement Services as referred to in Article 9 letter e consist of: legal assistance services include litigation legal assistance and support and non-litigation legal assistance and support;
law enforcement services include law enforcement at the police level, law enforcement at the prosecutor's office level, and law enforcement at the court level;
law enforcement services at the police level as referred to in letter b include law enforcement in the investigation and/or inquiry process;
law enforcement services at the prosecutor's office level as referred to in letter b include law enforcement in the pre-prosecution and prosecution process; and law enforcement services at the court level as referred to in letter b include law enforcement at the pre-trial stage, trial, and verdict pronouncement.

text:
Pasal 15
Pelayanan Pemulangan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 9 huruf f meliputi: pemulangan korban kekerasan berbasis gender dan anak;
pemulangan korban tindak pidana perdagangan orang.
Pelayanan Reintegrasi Sosial sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 9 huruf f meliputi: reintegrasi dengan keluarga;
reintegrasi dengan keluarga pengganti;
reintegrasi dengan lingkungan; dan reintegrasi pendidikan.

translated_text:
Article 15
Repatriation Services as referred to in Article 9 letter f include: repatriation of victims of gender-based violence and children;
repatriation of victims of criminal acts of human trafficking.
Social Reintegration Services as referred to in Article 9 letter f include: reintegration with family;
reintegration with substitute family;
reintegration with the environment; and reintegration of education.

text:
Pasal 16
Koordinasi  dan  kerjasama sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 9 huruf g meliputi: melakukan koordinasi dan kerjasama penanganan kasus kekerasan dengan UPPTK;
melakukan koordinasi dan kerjasama dengan pusat pelayanan terpadu antar kabupaten/kota; dan melakukan koordinasi dan kerjasama dengan lembaga-lembaga penyedia  layanan bagi korban kekerasan berbasis gender dan anak.

translated_text:
Article 16
Coordination and cooperation as referred to in Article 9 letter g includes: conducting coordination and cooperation in handling cases of violence with UPPTK;
conducting coordination and cooperation with integrated service centers between regencies/cities; and conducting coordination and cooperation with institutions providing services for victims of gender-based violence and children.

text:
Pasal 17
Peningkatan Partisipasi Masyarakat sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 9 huruf h dilakukan dengan cara: menumbuhkan kepedulian masyarakat terhadap kasus-kasus kekerasan berbasis gender dan anak;
mendorong masyarakat untuk berpartisipasi aktif dalam memberikan informasi dan melaporkan adanya kekerasan berbasis gender dan anak;
menumbuhkan kearifan lokal dalam penanganan kekerasan berbasis gender dan anak;
menyelenggarakan penguatan kelompok-kelompok masyarakat dalam   penanganan kekerasan berbasis gender dan anak; dan menyebarluaskan informasi tentang peraturan perundang-undangan yang berkaitan dengan kekerasan berbasis gender dan anak.

translated_text:
Article 17
Increasing Community Participation as referred to in Article 9 letter h is carried out by means of: fostering community awareness of cases of gender-based violence and violence against children;
encouraging the community to actively participate in providing information and reporting the occurrence of gender-based violence and violence against children;
fostering local wisdom in handling gender-based violence and violence against children;
organizing the strengthening of community groups in handling gender-based violence and violence against children; and disseminating information about laws and regulations related to gender-based violence and violence against children.

text:
Bagian Ketiga
UPPTK
Pasal 19
UPPTK sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 5 ayat (1) huruf b, dibentuk oleh Camat sesuai dengan ketentuan Peraturan Perundang-undangan.
UPPTK sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) keanggotaannya terdiri dari: unsur pemerintah kecamatan;
unsur kepolisian kecamatan;
unsur organisasi kemasyarakatan;
institusi pelayanan kesehatan;
tokoh masyarakat; dan tokoh agama.
Keanggotaan Tim UUPTK sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (2) ditetapkan dengan Keputusan Camat.

translated_text:
Part Three
UPPTK
Article 19
UPPTK as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (1) letter b, is formed by the Camat in accordance with the provisions of Laws and Regulations.
UPPTK as referred to in paragraph (1) consists of members from: sub-district government elements;
sub-district police elements;
community organization elements;
health service institutions;
community figures; and religious figures.
The membership of the UPPTK Team as referred to in paragraph (2) is established by Decree of the Camat.

text:
Pasal 20
UPPTK sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 5 ayat (1) huruf b mempunyai tugas: menerima pengaduan kasus kekerasan berbasis gender dan anak;
memberikan konsultasi awal kepada korban kekerasan berbasis gender dan anak;
melakukan intervensi krisis terhadap korban kekerasan berbasis gender dan anak; dan memberi rujukan penanganan kasus kekerasan berbasis gender dan anak kepada PPT PKBGA.

translated_text:
Article 20
UPPTK as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (1) letter b has the duties of: receiving complaints of gender-based and child violence cases;
providing initial consultation to victims of gender-based and child violence;
conducting crisis intervention for victims of gender-based and child violence; and providing referrals for handling gender-based and child violence cases to PPT PKBGA.

text:
Pasal 21
Dalam melaksanakan tugas sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 20, UPPTK mempunyai kewajiban: melakukan koordinasi dan konsultasi dengan PPT PKBGA;
mendokumentasikan dan melaporkan setiap kasus kekerasan berbasis gender dan anak yang ditanganinya kepada PPT PKBGA.

translated_text:
Article 21
In carrying out the duties as referred to in Article 20, UPPTK has the obligations: to coordinate and consult with PPT PKBGA;
to document and report every case of gender-based violence and violence against children handled to PPT PKBGA.

text:
Pasal 22
Setiap korban kekerasan berbasis gender dan anak berhak: memperoleh perlindungan atas keamanan pribadi, keluarga dan harta bendanya, serta bebas dari ancaman yang berkenaan dengan keterangan yang akan, sedang, atau telah diberikan;
untuk ikut serta dalam proses memilih dan menentukan bentuk perlindungan dan dukungan keamanan;
bebas dari pertanyaan yang menjerat;
mendapatkan informasi mengenai perkembangan kasus dan putusan pengadilan; dan mendapatkan layanan pengaduan, layanan kesehatan, layanan rehabilitasi sosial, layanan bantuan dan penegakan hukum, serta layanan pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial.
Hak korban sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilaksanakan sesuai dengan ketentuan Peraturan Perundang-undangan.

translated_text:
Article 22
Every victim of gender-based violence and children has the right to: obtain protection for personal security, family and property, and freedom from threats related to testimony that will be, is being, or has been given;
to participate in the process of selecting and determining the form of protection and security support;
freedom from ensnaring questions;
obtain information regarding case developments and court decisions; and obtain complaint services, health services, social rehabilitation services, legal aid and enforcement services, as well as repatriation and social reintegration services.
The rights of victims as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in accordance with the provisions of Laws and Regulations.

text:
Pasal 25
Pemerintah Daerah berkewajiban dan bertanggung jawab untuk melaksanakan upaya perlindungan korban kekerasan dalam bentuk: mencegah terjadinya segala bentuk kekerasan berbasis gender dan anak;
memberikan perlindungan dengan menyediakan layanan pengaduan, layanan kesehatan, layanan rehabilitasi sosial, layanan bantuan dan penegakan hukum, layanan pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial, mengupayakan peningkatan partisipasi masyarakat, serta monitoring dan pelaporan;
mendorong dan meningkatkan partisipasi masyarakat; dan melakukan kerjasama dengan penyedia layanan dalam upaya pencegahan, perlindungan, dan pemulihan korban kekerasan.
Untuk melaksanakan kewajiban sebagaimana dan tanggung jawab dimaksud pada ayat (1), Pemerintah Daerah mempunyai kewenangan untuk: merumuskan kebijakan dan program tentang penghapusan kekerasan berbasis gender dan anak;
membentuk pusat pelayanan terpadu;
membentuk lembaga pelayanan pengaduan di tingkat kecamatan;
memfasilitasi terselenggaranya pusat pelayanan terpadu dan kegiatan lembaga pelayanan pengaduan di tingkat kecamatan;
menyediakan sarana dan prasarana;
meningkatkan kapasitas lembaga penyedia layanan;
melakukan koordinasi dan kerjasama dalam penyelenggaraan perlindungan terhadap korban kekerasan berbasis gender dan anak;
mendorong dan meningkatkan partisipasi masyarakat; dan melakukan monitoring dan evaluasi.
Dalam pelaksanaan kewajiban, tanggung jawab, dan kewenangannya, Bupati dapat mendelegasikan kepada Perangkat Daerah.
Perangkat Daerah menerima pendelegasian dari Bupati sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (3) dalam pelaksanaannya menyusun Rencana Aksi Daerah untuk perlindungan korban.
Pemerintah Daerah dalam melaksanakan kewajiban sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dan ayat (2) harus memperhatikan hak dan kewajiban orangtua, wali, suami, istri, atau orang lain yang secara hukum bertanggung jawab kepada korban.

translated_text:
Article 25
The Regional Government has the obligation and responsibility to implement protection efforts for victims of violence in the form of: preventing the occurrence of all forms of gender-based violence and violence against children;
providing protection by supplying complaint services, health services, social rehabilitation services, legal aid and enforcement services, repatriation and social reintegration services, seeking to increase community participation, as well as monitoring and reporting;
encouraging and increasing community participation; and conducting cooperation with service providers in efforts to prevent, protect, and recover victims of violence.
To implement the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government has the authority to: formulate policies and programs on the elimination of gender-based violence and violence against children;
establish integrated service centers;
establish complaint service institutions at the sub-district level;
facilitate the implementation of integrated service centers and activities of complaint service institutions at the sub-district level;
provide facilities and infrastructure;
increase the capacity of service provider institutions;
conduct coordination and cooperation in the implementation of protection for victims of gender-based violence and violence against children;
encourage and increase community participation; and conduct monitoring and evaluation.
In the implementation of its obligations, responsibilities, and authorities, the Regent may delegate to Regional Apparatus.
Regional Apparatus receiving delegation from the Regent as referred to in paragraph (3) shall in its implementation prepare a Regional Action Plan for victim protection.
The Regional Government in implementing obligations as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) must pay attention to the rights and obligations of parents, guardians, husbands, wives, or other persons who are legally responsible for the victim.

text:
Pasal 26
Masyarakat, keluarga, dan orangtua mempunyai kewajiban dan tanggung jawab:
a. 	mencegah terjadinya kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak;
b. 	melaporkan bila terjadi kekerasan;
c. 	melindungi korban; dan
d. 	memberikan pertolongan darurat.

translated_text:
Article 26
The community, family, and parents have the obligation and responsibility to:
a. 	prevent the occurrence of violence against women and children;
b. 	report if violence occurs;
c. 	protect victims; and
d. 	provide emergency assistance.

text:
BAB VI
PERAN SERTA MASYARAKAT
Pasal 27
Masyarakat dapat berperan serta membantu upaya pencegahan dan penanganan korban kekerasan berbasis gender dan anak.
Peran serta masyarakat sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) berupa: memberikan informasi dan/atau melaporkan setiap kekerasan yang diketahuinya;
memberikan perlindungan bagi korban;
memberikan pertolongan darurat;
memberikan advokasi terhadap korban dan atau masyarakat tentang penanganan kekerasan berbasis gender dan anak;
membantu proses pengajuan permohonan penetapan perlindungan; dan membantu dalam proses pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial.
Peran serta masyarakat sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dapat dilakukan oleh perorangan, lembaga sosial kemasyarakatan, lembaga swadaya masyarakat, lembaga pendidikan, lembaga keagamaan, swasta, dan media massa.

translated_text:
CHAPTER VI
COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION
Article 27
The community may participate in assisting prevention efforts and handling of victims of gender-based violence and children.
Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be in the form of: providing information and/or reporting any violence that comes to their knowledge;
providing protection for victims;
providing emergency assistance;
providing advocacy to victims and or the community regarding the handling of gender-based violence and children;
assisting in the process of submitting applications for protection orders; and assisting in the repatriation and social reintegration process.
Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) may be carried out by individuals, social community institutions, non-governmental organizations, educational institutions, religious institutions, the private sector, and mass media.

text:
Pasal 4
Huruf a Yang dimaksud dengan kekerasan fisik adalah setiap perbuatan yang mengakibatkan rasa sakit, cedera, luka atau cacat pada tubuh seseorang, gugurnya kandungan, pingsan dan/atau menyebabkan kematian.
Huruf b Kekerasan psikis adalah setiap perbuatan yang mengakibatkan ketakutan, hilangnya rasa percaya diri, hilangnya kemampuan untuk bertindak, rasa tidak berdaya dan/atau penderitaan psikis berat pada seseorang.
Huruf c Kekerasan seksual adalah setiap perbuatan yang berupa pelecehan seksual, pemaksaan hubungan seksual, pemaksaan hubungan seksual dengan orang lain untuk tujuan komersial dan/atau tujuan tertentu.
Huruf d Penelantaran adalah: perbuatan yang mengakibatkan tidak terpenuhinya kebutuhan anak secara wajar, baik fisik, mental, spiritual maupun sosial yang dilakukan oleh orangtua, wali, atau pihak lain manapun yang bertanggung jawab atas pengasuhannya;
perbuatan mengabaikan dengan sengaja untuk memelihara, merawat, atau mengurus anak sebagaimana mestinya yang dilakukan oleh orangtua, wali, atau  pihak  lain manapun yang bertanggung jawab atas pengasuhannya;
perbuatan yang menelantarkan orang dalam lingkup rumah tangganya; dan/atau perbuatan yang mengakibatkan ketergantungan ekonomi dengan cara membatasi dan/atau melarang untuk bekerja yang layak di dalam atau di luar rumah sehingga korban berada dibawah kendali orang tersebut.
Huruf e Kekerasan lainnya merupakan setiap perbuatan yang disebabkan karena: ancaman kekerasan, yang meliputi setiap perbuatan secara melawan hukum berupa ucapan, tulisan, gambar, simbol, atau gerakan tubuh, baik dengan atau tanpa menggunakan sarana yang menimbulkan rasa takut atau mengekang kebebasan hakiki seseorang;
b.	pemaksaan, yang meliputi suatu keadaan dimana seseorang/korban disuruh melakukan sesuatu sedemikian rupa sehingga orang itu melakukan sesuatu yang berlawanan dengan kehendak sendiri.

translated_text:
Article 4
Letter a Physical violence is any act that results in pain, injury, wounds or disability to a person's body, miscarriage, unconsciousness and/or causes death.
Letter b Psychological violence is any act that results in fear, loss of self-confidence, loss of ability to act, feelings of helplessness and/or severe psychological suffering to a person.
Letter c Sexual violence is any act in the form of sexual harassment, forced sexual intercourse, forced sexual intercourse with others for commercial purposes and/or certain purposes.
Letter d Neglect is: an act that results in the failure to fulfill the needs of a child properly, whether physical, mental, spiritual or social, committed by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
an act of deliberately neglecting to maintain, care for, or look after a child as appropriate, committed by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
an act of neglecting a person within the scope of their household; and/or an act that results in economic dependence by means of restricting and/or prohibiting proper work inside or outside the home so that the victim is under the control of that person.
Letter e Other violence constitutes any act caused by: threat of violence, which includes any unlawful act in the form of speech, writing, images, symbols, or body movements, whether with or without using means that create fear or restrict a person's fundamental freedom;
b.	coercion, which includes a situation where a person/victim is ordered to do something in such a way that the person does something contrary to their own will.
